# Contracts

`contracts/` is the fixed boundary between the Rust shell, the React UI and the orchestrator. It changes only with an ADR and a version tag.

## Layout

```
contracts/
  schemas/        # Zod v4: envelope.ts, cards/*.ts, attention.ts, ledger.ts, session.ts, events.ts
  a2a/            # state-map.ts  (A2A task state -> UI state)
  bindings/       # generated by tauri-specta (bindings.ts: commands + events); committed; never hand-edited
  fixtures/       # every card type x { populated, loading, empty, error, expired }; three scripted journeys
  CHANGELOG.md    # one entry per contracts@x.y tag
```

## Card envelope (every card)

```ts
export const CardEnvelope = z.object({
  cardId: z.string().uuid(),
  agentId: z.string(),           // registry id, e.g. "servicenow-itsm"
  journeyId: z.string().uuid(),
  taskId: z.string().optional(), // A2A task
  createdAt: z.iso.datetime(),
  type: z.enum(['summary','record','table','choice','confirmation','link']),
});
```

Per-type payloads extend the envelope with `z.discriminatedUnion('type', [...])`. The six types are closed; a new type is a contract minor bump and a renderer PR in the same change.

## Attention

- Request: `{ attentionId, journeyId, kind: 'confirm'|'choose'|'provide', title, requester, subject, evidence[], options[] (2-3), allowFreeText, expiresAt }`.
- Decision: `{ attentionId, decision: optionId | 'reject', freeText?, decidedAt, idempotencyKey }`. Idempotency key is generated by the UI once per decision attempt and reused on retry.
- Expired items are read-only; the schema carries `state: 'open'|'decided'|'expired'`.

## A2A state map (`a2a/state-map.ts`)

| A2A task state | UI state |
|---|---|
| `submitted`, `working` | progress (thread shows handoff chip + skeleton) |
| `input-required` | Attention item (kind from message) |
| `auth-required` | Attention item, kind `confirm`, auth flavour |
| `completed` | cards from artifacts |
| `failed`, `rejected`, `canceled` | `summary` card with `tone: 'failure'` |

The dock never speaks A2A to sub-agents; it talks to the orchestrator API. This map is for interpreting orchestrator events.

## Ledger view model (Recent)

`{ eventId, eventType: 'proposed'|'confirmed'|'executed'|'failed'|'cancelled'|'expired', occurredAt, journeyId, agentId, platform, action, object: { type, id, label, link }, summary, actor: { userId, displayName } }`. Only the orchestrator emits `confirmed`.

## Rules

- Zod is the source of truth; TypeScript types are `z.infer`. Never write a type by hand that a schema already defines.
- Every schema has a fixture for every state, and every fixture passes `schema.parse` in `contracts/schemas/__tests__/`.
- Unknown fields: `.strict()` on decisions we send; `.passthrough()` on cards we receive (forward compatibility), but unknown `type` values are rejected.
- Bindings drift check: CI runs `cargo run --bin export-bindings` and fails if `git diff --exit-code contracts/bindings`.
- Versioning: tag `contracts@MAJOR.MINOR`. Minor = additive (new optional field, new fixture). Major = anything else. The orchestrator team signs off every tag in `CHANGELOG.md`.
